# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Component Authoring Standards

_Examples below reference the original {{SYSTEM_NAME}} system; the patterns are system-agnostic._

DS-fidelity + Figma-optimization rules for **building or editing any {{BRAND_SHORT}} {{SYSTEM_NAME}}
component** (`{{DS_FIGMA_KEY}}`). Every new/changed component must meet these
so the library stays optimized, themeable, and consistent. Pairs with
`skills/ds-components.md` (what exists) + `manifest/manifest.schema.md` (ground truth)
+ `skills/figma-gotchas.md` (API pitfalls).

> **Note:** the "Audit baseline" section below is a real {{SYSTEM_NAME}} snapshot kept as a worked
> example of how to record an authoring audit; replace it with your own once you run one.

> **Quick gate before publishing any component — the 10-point check:**
> 1 token-bound · 2 right variant/prop split · 3 auto-layout · 4 nested instances
> exposed · 5 instance-swaps for variable content · 6 clean icons · 7 text styles ·
> 8 naming · 9 AA + 44px targets · 10 description/Code Connect + manifest logged.

---

## 1. Variables, tokens & modes
- **Bind every visible fill / stroke / effect color to a Semantic token** — never a
  raw hex. Layer order is `1. Primitives → 2. Tokens → 3. Semantic`; **components
  bind to `3. Semantic` only** (never to a primitive/raw value).
- **Bind spacing, radius, and sizing to number variables** where the DS provides
  them (e.g. `Scale/*`, `Border-Radius/*`). Don't hardcode 16/24/etc. when a token exists.
- **Theme with modes, not duplicate tokens.** Semantic tokens should carry their
  light/dark values as **variable modes** on the `3. Semantic` collection, so a
  component themes by mode-switch. Do **not** spin up parallel `*/Inverse` tokens for
  dark — that's the anti-pattern the current file fell into (see Backlog P1-A).
- **Set `variable.scopes` explicitly** when creating variables (never leave
  `ALL_SCOPES`) — e.g. `TEXT_FILL` for text colors, `FRAME_FILL/SHAPE_FILL` for
  surfaces, `GAP/WIDTH_HEIGHT/CORNER_RADIUS` for numbers.
- **Gradients can't bind to variables** (Figma limitation) — match the hex to the
  token value and note it. This is the only sanctioned raw-color exception.

## 2. Variants vs component properties — avoid variant explosion
The variant count is the **product** of every variant axis's options. Keep it small.
- **VARIANT axes** only for things that change visual *structure/appearance*:
  `Appearance`, `Type`, `Size`, `Status`, `State` (when states differ structurally).
- **BOOLEAN properties** for show/hide and on/off: `Selected`, `Disabled`,
  `Show Icon`, `Show Divider`, `Show Trailing`. Never make these a variant axis.
- **INSTANCE_SWAP properties** for swappable content: icons, illustrations, avatars,
  nested buttons. Seed `preferredValues`.
- **TEXT properties** for every editable string.
- **Never make a nested instance's own attribute a top-level variant** — e.g. an
  `Icon Size` axis multiplies the entire set just to resize a nested glyph. Drive it
  from the nested icon instead (swap to a sized icon / the icon's own size).
- **Flag any set > ~24 variants** for review — it almost always hides a
  collapsible axis (see Backlog P1-B: Button = 144).

## 3. Auto layout
- **Every container, row, and stack uses auto layout.** Absolute positioning only for
  true overlays (scrims, decorative glows) via `layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE'`, and
  for icon bounding boxes.
- Use **FILL / HUG** sizing intentionally; set `layoutSizing*='FILL'` **after**
  `appendChild` (Plugin API rule).
- Reach for modern AL features where they fit: **min/max width**, **wrap**, and
  absolute children inside an AL frame.
- **Anchor optional elements** so toggling `Show X` doesn't collapse/shift siblings.

## 4. Nested instances & exposure
- **Expose** (`isExposedInstance = true`) any nested instance a consumer will
  customize — leading/trailing icons, action buttons, avatars, tab items, illustrations
  — so they can swap/edit it **without detaching** the parent.
- Bind each nested swappable visual to a **set-level `INSTANCE_SWAP`** prop and expose it.
- **Re-point nested instances to canonical sets** — no duplicate/orphan main
  components (a recurring cleanup; see manifest patches `[14,16]`).

## 5. Icons
- Glyph color = an **`Icon/*` semantic token** (not a `Text/*` token).
- The icon **`Bounding box` rectangle MUST be transparent (no fill)** — never leave
  Figma's default `#d9d9d9`. A filled bounding box renders as a stray gray square when
  the icon is placed/recolored sparsely (see Backlog P1-D).
- When recoloring an icon, **recolor only the glyph `VECTOR`(s)** — skip the bounding box.

## 6. Text
- **Bind every text node to a text style** (`Title/*`, `Body/*`, `Caption/*`,
  `Button/Label-*`) — never raw font family/size/line-height.
- Text fill = a **`Text/*` token**.
- Set `textAutoResize` intentionally: `HEIGHT` + `FILL` width to wrap and grow;
  `WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT` only for genuine single-line labels (it hug-centers in AL).

## 7. Naming
- Variant axes: clear PascalCase names + readable options (`State=Default`, not `s=0`).
- Layers: meaningful (`Leading`, `Title`, `Trailing`, `Divider`, `Icon Glyph`), never
  `Frame 23` / `Rectangle 5`.
- Component + set names match `aps-components.md` and manifest `keyComponents`.

## 8. Accessibility (bake in, don't bolt on)
- **WCAG AA contrast**: text ≥ 4.5:1 (normal) / 3:1 (≥24px or bold ≥19px); icons &
  UI boundaries ≥ 3:1. Check **every State and variant**, not just the default.
- **Touch targets ≥ 44px** (Fitts). Apply the `workflow_design-qa-sweep` lens
  (a11y + Fitts + Nielsen + UX-laws) on every new/changed component.

## 9. Handoff — use modern Figma features
- **Component Description** on every set: what it is, when to use, prop summary.
- **Dev-mode Annotations** for non-obvious behavior/states.
- **Code Connect** mappings where engineering consumes the component.
- **Changelog frame** (in-file) + manifest `patches[]` entry on every change.

## 10. Publish discipline
- The **Plugin API can't publish** (Critical Rule #1) — a human clicks *Publish
  library*. Source edits don't reach consumers until republish; `importComponentByKeyAsync`
  returns the last *published* version.
- After a republish, **consumer instances can be stuck on a stale cached local main**
  and won't auto-pull — `swapComponent` them onto the freshly-imported remote (learned
  on the List-with-Button + Card rollouts).

